00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:17.120
Construction of Tesla's dedicated, Optimus Factory at Giga, Texas

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:22.260
marks the first physical step towards scaling humanoid robot production at volume.

00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:27.520
Drone footage from May 27th shows the first steel structure now standing

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:33.600
on the north campus of Giga Factory, Texas. The dedicated facility is designed to support production

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:39.960
of up to 10 million Optimus units. Phase two work is already visible alongside the initial framing.

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:46.440
The move shifts Optimus from prototype development into a purpose-built manufacturing footprint.

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:51.840
Next milestone to watch is when equipment installation begins inside the new structure.

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:57.700
Construction of a 10 million unit factory shifts the robot program from research

00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:03.120
possibility to manufacturing throughput problem. The decision to allocate prime Giga

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:08.700
Texas real estate and begin steel erection signals that production scaling is now treated as an

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:14.560
